(Reading exactly fills a fixed-size buffer should not raise an error)

open a file for writing called out at "./tmp_exact_fit.txt".
Write "hello" to out.
Close out.

open a file for reading called inp at "./tmp_exact_fit.txt".
a buffer called b is 5 bytes in size.
Read from inp into b.
On error Print "error".
Print b's size.
Close inp.

Delete the file "./tmp_exact_fit.txt".
